  "facts": [
    "The Sozina Tunnel, 4,189 meters long, opened on 13 July 2005, the same day Montenegro celebrated its national day, marking a milestone in the country’s infrastructure development.",
    "Built at a cost of 70 million euros, the Sozina Tunnel is the longest and most modern vehicular tunnel in Montenegro, surpassing even the older 6 km train tunnel.",
    "Since 15 July 2005, an open toll system collects fees at the tunnel entrance, making the 25‑kilometer shortcut between Podgorica and Bar a one‑hour drive."
